{"title":"*Violent Saviors*","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/927429773/0/marginalrevolution~Violent-Saviors.html","date":1762720005000,"content":"<p>That is the new William Easterly book, and the subtitle is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Violent-Saviors-Wests-Conquest-Rest/dp/1541675754/ref=sr_1_1?crid=25K9F83MMMSBC&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.TJHjBndsVM2wlTQRIMm_ImP9q886FomHCUTjKBBG5dekwJl15g0jrsyQ555VTZZl8xg_GkaullPf20SkuwxaZqUXkVV8CGfDkG_arupYOMXgjgtumb5Q1bdlhWYDEK0XE4eom4-BZ_E42Yj-gDO9ojYH-jaokY3OfTSXMRS-UmMdD9srFNo0x7JcXCoy0Fmw.m9XYIVw_qcfsuXppOi37dSyJ2BQQ1cZNEch5zJmLglc&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=violent+saviors&amp;qid=1762701759&amp;sprefix=violent+saviors%2Caps%2C120&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">The West’s Conquest of the Rest</a>.  I liked this book very much, but found the title and also book jacket and descriptions misleading.  I think of this work as a full-throated examination and study of the classical liberal anti-imperialist tradition.  We have been needing such a thing for a long time.  It is not that I expected Easterly to be poorly informed, but it amazes me how well he knows this material from a historical point of view.  A lengthy (and good) discussion of E.D. Morel!</p>\r\n<p>So recommended, and here’s hoping these traditions find some new legs and less crazy adherents.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/violent-saviors.html\">*Violent Saviors*</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/927429773/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/927429773/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.